From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: drop boost_system from the link list

  x86_64-webos-linux-ld: cannot find -lboost_system

Boost.System has been header-only since Boost 1.69 and Boost 1.90 ships no
compiled library at all, so this bare entry asks the linker for something that
does not exist. What it used to provide is inline in the headers now.

boost_filesystem here, and boost_regex in resource_manager, are still real
compiled libraries in 1.90 and are left alone.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/server/CMakeLists.txt | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/server/CMakeLists.txt b/src/server/CMakeLists.txt
index 8e96004..c5e187d 100644
--- a/src/server/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/server/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -39,7 +39,6 @@ set(
    ums_connector
    ums_connector_impl
    ums_registry
-   boost_system
    boost_filesystem
 
    ${GLIB2_LIBRARIES}
